sequenceDiagram
    title BLE Central Bonded Reconnection: Re-encrypt with Stored Keys

    participant Product as Product
    participant CN as CN<br>[implements GapCentral]
    participant Peripheral as BLE Peripheral

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over Product, Peripheral: 1. Locate the bonded peripheral (optional)
        opt Product does not already know the target and scans first
            Product->>CN: GapCentral.StartDeviceDiscovery()
            CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.CurrentState(scanning)
            CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.DeviceDiscovered(<br>addressWithType={address=6C:8B:2F:3A:9D:41, addressType=randomAddress},<br>rssi=-42)
            Product->>CN: GapCentral.Standby()
            CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.CurrentState(standby)
        end

        Note over Product: Alternatively, Connect(bond.identityAddress) directly.<br>The controller matches incoming/observed RPAs via the LL resolving list<br>(populated with the peer's IRK at bond time).
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over Product, Peripheral: 2. Reconnect
        Product->>CN: GapCentral.Connect(<br>addressWithType={address=6C:8B:2F:3A:9D:41, addressType=randomAddress},<br>initiatingTimeoutInMs=5000)
        CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.CurrentState(initiating)
        CN->>Peripheral: BLE connection request
        Peripheral-->>CN: Connection accepted
        CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.CurrentState(connected)
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over Product, Peripheral: 3. Re-encryption
        Product->>CN: GapCentral.PairAndBond()
        CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.NumberOfBondsChanged(1)
        CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.PairingResult(pairedSuccessfully=true)

        Note over Product: PairAndBond is required. Without it the link stays unencrypted.<br>Existing bond is reused, so no SMP user interaction (no AuthenticationRequired).<br>NumberOfBondsChanged signals the LRU aging update — the bond count is unchanged.
    end
